# dev deploy target host key. Public — pinned, not secret.
#
# Verified 2026-09-04 (INF-068). Provenance, because it is the whole value of
# this file: the key was read directly from `/etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub`
# on the DEV host itself, by a session running on that host — not fetched over
# the network, and NOT via `ssh-keyscan`. A scan answers with whatever is at the
# other end, which is the question this file exists to answer, not the answer.
#
#   ssh-keygen -lf /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub
#   256 SHA256:ZbQ/hxxRx3LZUose3wqoRi+aQNQx/ohMPoBAFHf2uRo no comment (ED25519)
#
# The same key, byte for byte, that INF-034 verified out of band on 2026-08-29
# and pinned as `vps-dev.gogo.id.vn` (see the historical entry at the bottom).
# That match is itself evidence: the DEV host did not change on 2026-09-04 — what
# changed was the hostname the deploy reaches it by, and our description of where
# it lives. Two names, one machine, one key.
#
# The hostname is `ssh-dev.gogo.id.vn` because the deploy now connects through
# the Cloudflare Tunnel with Access in front (INF-068): a GitHub-hosted runner
# has no route to 192.168.68.68. Access authenticates the *connection*; this file
# authenticates the *host*. Neither substitutes for the other, and
# StrictHostKeyChecking stays `yes` against this file — if the key ever stops
# matching, the deploy must stop, not adapt.
ssh-dev.gogo.id.vn ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIArdTaRB2NkQ/qEcsl4JmvsMNAUWooqO4QewhoVf/JX1

# Historical, kept for the record and deliberately inert — a commented line is
# never consulted. `vps-dev.gogo.id.vn` was the public A record that reached this
# same host before the tunnel path replaced it. Same fingerprint as above.
# SHA256:ZbQ/hxxRx3LZUose3wqoRi+aQNQx/ohMPoBAFHf2uRo
# Verified out of band against the host, 2026-08-29. INF-034.
# vps-dev.gogo.id.vn:22 SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_10.2
# vps-dev.gogo.id.vn ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIArdTaRB2NkQ/qEcsl4JmvsMNAUWooqO4QewhoVf/JX1
